# Local env files: cover every .env* shape, while keeping the template tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Vercel's project linkage (the org and project ids live in here).
.vercel/

# Editor directories and files.
#
# The whole of .vscode/, including extensions.json — which the Vite scaffold
# deliberately keeps versioned so a clone gets the Volar recommendation. That
# trade only pays off on a repository with more than one developer on it. Here
# it put an editor's folder in the tree in exchange for a suggestion VS Code
# already makes on its own the moment it opens a .vue file.
#
# The file is still on disk and still works. It is simply not this project's
# business to carry it.
.vscode/
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Local tooling config
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# Affinity Designer sources: the editable original behind an exported asset, not
# something the site ships.
*.af

# Design reference material — the .dc.html prototypes, their runtime, and the
# asset folders they load from. All of it now lives outside the project, in
# `krub brand/reference/`, since the spec is written and nothing needs
# measuring against them any more.
#
# These rules stay as a guard: if a copy is ever dragged back in to check a
# value, it will not end up in a commit. The leading slashes matter — they
# anchor to the repository root so `public/assets` and `public/icons` are
# unaffected.
Home.dc.html
Design System.dc.html
support.js
/assets/
/icons/
/uploads/

# Playwright
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/playwright/.cache/

